WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.160
Marilla knows how big Anne can make the smallest thing, and she isn't wrong about

2
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:06.480
that.

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:12.160
When you're not sure where to start a summary, try a frame that a lot of readers

4
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:12.460
use.

5
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:20.000
Somebody wanted something, but something got in the way, so they did something, then

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.920
it ended a certain way.

7
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.800
Somebody, wanted, but, so, then.

8
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:31.040
If you can fill in those five words for a chapter, you have a solid summary, and the

9
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.200
fun extras have nowhere to go.

10
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.800
Try it once for Chapter 27 and once for Chapter 28.

11
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.160
Also watch for your own opinion sneaking in.

12
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.160
A summary tells what happened.

13
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:48.080
What you think about Anne's choices belongs in your answers on the Assignment tab.

